# Build context for the root `Containerfile` (the e2e lab's acme-proxy image).
#
# An allowlist, not a blocklist. The blocklist this replaced named nine paths and
# was wrong in both directions: it let `doc/` (12 MB), `CHANGELOG.md`, `CLAUDE.md`,
# `config.toml.example` and `rfc/` into the context, so editing prose invalidated
# `COPY . .` and forced a full rebuild of the crate; and `*.key`/`ca.pem` match
# only at the root, so `data/ca.key`, `data/ca.pem` and `data/sqlite.db` were
# copied into a build layer. A blocklist has to be extended for every directory
# the repository grows; this does not.
#
# What `cargo build` actually reads:
#   Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock  — the manifest and the pinned graph (`--locked`)
#   src/                     — including the assets `include_str!`ed from it
#                              (src/webadmin/static/, src/webadmin/templates/,
#                              src/notify/templates/)
#   migrations/              — `sqlx::migrate!()` in src/sqlite/db.rs
#
# `tests/` is deliberately absent: the only thing outside `src/` it is reached for
# is `tests/fixtures/rsa_test_key.pk8`, `include_bytes!`d from the `#[cfg(test)]`
# module in src/extractors/signature.rs, which a non-test build never compiles.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!src/
!migrations/
